{"tool_name":"novowrap","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"novowrap","home":"https://github.com/wpwupingwp/novowrap","license":"AGPL-3.0","summary":"NOVOWrap is an automated solution for plastid genome assembly and structure standardization.","addition_date":"2021-10-25T08:06:18.402778Z","last_update_date":"2021-10-25T08:07:01.477388Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:novowrap","credit":[{"email":"slzhou@ibcas.ac.cn","name":"Shiliang Zhou","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Sequence assembly validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3180"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"NOVOWrap","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1111/1755-0998.13410","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 John Wiley & Sons Ltd.Plastid genomes play an important role in genomics and evolutionary biology. Next-generation sequencing has revolutionized plastid genomic data acquisition to the point that genome assembly has become a bottleneck for widespread utilization of plastid genome data. To solve this problem, we developed an open-source, cross-platform tool known as, NOVOWrap, which includes both command-line and graphical interfaces for automatically assembling plastid genomes on personal computers. With minimal inputs, settings, and user intervention, NOVOWrap can automatically assemble plastid genomes, validate results and standardize the structure using affordable computer resources. The performance of this software has been successfully benchmarked against the plastid genomes of 11 species belonging to lycopods, gymnosperms, and angiosperms. By liberating researchers from laborious and cumbersome computer manipulations and create reliable and standardized genomic data, NOVOWrap is expected to accelerate plastid genome assembly, ease the process of data exchange, and contribute to downstream analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Chen H."},{"name":"Wu P."},{"name":"Xu C."},{"name":"Yang J."},{"name":"Zhang X."},{"name":"Zhou S."}],"date":"2021-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Molecular Ecology Resources","title":"NOVOWrap: An automated solution for plastid genome assembly and structure standardization"},"pmid":"33934526","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Plant biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0780"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"NOVOWrap","home":"https://bio.tools/novowrap","license":"AGPL-3.0","summary":"NOVOWrap is an automated solution for plastid genome assembly and structure standardization.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:novowrap/app/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":30,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":5,"year":"2022"},{"count":7,"year":"2023"},{"count":7,"year":"2025"},{"count":10,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.1111/1755-0998.13410","pmid":"33934526","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"NOVOWrap: An automated solution for plastid genome assembly and structure standard